    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Lemma 8.1.6. Suppose ℓ = 2 and (ℓ,n!) = 1 if we are in case O1. If φ ∈ Φss(G∗,Fℓ) is a generic semi-simple toral L-parameter, and µ ∈ X•(G∗) is a dominant cocharacter, then φ is µ-regular."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 2,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 453.108, 767.968, 463.068, 768.448 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "2503.04623_pg54_images/imageFile1.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "caption",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Caption",
    "id" : 3,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 721.209, 523.255, 744.531 ],
    "linked content id" : 4,
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Italic",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Similarly, if φ♯ ∈ Φss(G♯,Fℓ) is a generic semi-simple toral L-parameter, and µ♯ ∈ X•(G♯) is a dominant cocharacter such that (ℓ,n!) = 1 if we are in case O1, then φ♯ is µ♯-regular."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 204.828, 743.728, 214.788, 744.208 ],
